      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im trying to integrate this stripe api for my side project but im getting a 402 error on the payment intent creation even though i know the card is good. what are the common reasons for a 402 and how should i go about checking my request payload to see if im missing something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The 402 error code, also known as a \"payment method\" error, typically occurs when Stripe receives an insufficient funds error or an error with the card's billing cycle repeat option. To diagnose the issue, check the following:\n\n* Make sure the customer has a valid card number, expiration date, and CVV.\n* Verify that the card's billing cycle repeat option is set correctly for the current payment period.\n* Ensure the Stripe account payment method is up-to-date and approved.\n\nTry validating these factors in your request payload and verify the customer's credit card information matches the details provided during account setup.",
