      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the card details and they seem fine, and the account is active. i'm looking at my logs now and the payload looks like it's sending all the right fields (amount, currency, customer id, etc). is there any way the specific way the error is being triggered could hint at a configuration issue on the stripe dashboard side rather than just the card itself? like maybe some weird restriction on the merchant account?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, that's a good angle to explore. A 402 error can also indicate configuration issues with your Stripe account, such as:\n\n* A high-risk merchant account status: If your account has been flagged as high-risk for suspicious activity, Stripe may be applying additional verification steps or restrictions.\n* Inadequate setup of Stripe's webhooks: Ensure that Stripe's webhooks are set up to notify your application when a payment intent is created, and that your application is configured to receive and process these webhooks.\n* Insufficient country-specific settings: Some country-specific settings, such as the maximum fee threshold, might be causing the error.\n\nDouble-check your Stripe dashboard to ensure that these settings are correctly configured.",
